course: dictionary
lesson: 6081
title: Metal: a hard, shiny material
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Metal is a hard, shiny material like iron, steel, gold, silver, copper or aluminium. Coins, nails and keys are made of metal.
explain: Metal can also describe something. «A metal spoon» is a spoon made of metal. The word before or after it often tells you which meaning is being used.
explain: Context gives clues. «A can of soda left too long in the freezer can bulge and burst» shows that metal things can be affected by cold, so you can think about what the metal is like and what it does.
fact: Metal is a hard, shiny material.
fact: Iron, steel, gold, silver, copper and aluminium are all metals.
fact: Most metals let heat and electricity pass through them easily.
fact: Iron is attracted by a magnet, but not all metals are.
fact: Metal pots and spoons get hot, so never put metal in a microwave or into a socket.
exercise: Which of these is a metal? | Cotton | Plastic | *Copper | Wood
exercise: «A metal spoon» uses metal to describe the spoon. What does it mean? | *Made of metal | Very heavy to lift | Found under the sea | Shiny like a mirror only
exercise: «Where hands rub a brass door knob every day, the metal stays bright.» Which word tells you the metal is shiny? | knob | rubbed | layer | *bright
test: In «a metal spoon», what kind of word is metal? | Noun | *Adjective | Verb
test: Why should you never put metal in a microwave? | Because it makes the food cold | Because it makes the food sweeter | *Because it can make sparks and cause damage
exam: Which of these is NOT a metal? | Steel | *Wood | Gold | Iron
